{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"File impact corrected — 12 paths pointed at a directory that no longer exists.\n\nWhile amending AC5 I checked the recorded `file_impact` against the tree and found 12 of the 44 entries still naming `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/`. That directory has **0 tracked files**:\n\n    $ git ls-files 'tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/*' | wc -l\n    0\n\nThe modules live at `tests/unit/reconciler/` — the rename the Context paragraph already describes as LANDED. The description was updated for that rename; the `file_impact` array was not, so the two disagreed.\n\nThis matters at close rather than now. The completion gate reads `file_impact` to decide which paths the landed commit must have touched, so 12 entries naming a path no commit can touch would have produced a confident, line-cited failure on work that is in fact complete.\n\nCorrected, and `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` added for the AC5 drain, bringing the array to **45** entries:\n\n- 12 `rebar_reconciler/` → `reconciler/` (6 pairs: 2 under `diffing/`, 3 under `state/`, 1 at the package root)\n- 1 new: `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`, reason \"AC5 drain: `--update-stale` removes the 1 stale `_clean` row for the deleted twin\"\n- The 32 `tests/unit/metrics/` and `tests/unit/workflow/` entries were already correct and are unchanged\n\nThe reason text on the deleted `test_backend_scalar_surface_heldout.py` entry also changed, from \"its `_clean` autouse key buckets stale\" to \"its `_clean` autouse key is drained from the mechanism baseline,\" so it matches the amended AC5 rather than the superseded wording.\n\nScope note: amending the description makes the existing plan-review attestation `stale-material`, so a fresh `review-plan` is required before this ticket can close. That is the gate's rule for a material edit, and the edit was necessary — the previous AC5 was unsatisfiable alongside AC6.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793501708188816912,"uuid":"a5e6429d-168d-4b40-a25e-9e55234050f9"}